Z||000000||3fifty||09-29-2001||01:16 AM||||The rest of the parts to complete my Archie<BR>Master Install Kit should be arriving soon.<BR>I hope to have the LM-1 crate motor in and running within the next 4 or 5 months. I know<BR>that the Diablo and Countach will hold more straight on the road because of the extended length. With aprox 260 hp, fresh auto tranny,10" tires on the rear, and stock<BR>wheelbase, should I expect to grip and go or<BR>spin when I punch the pedal at about 30mph or so? I am not going to hole shot and start breaking things. Thanks, 3fifty ||||reg||5
Z||000001||California Kid||09-29-2001||10:00 AM||||It's just going to grip and go, no tire spin, handling will be same as it was with the V6. May be just a bit ass heavy if your using a V8 with iron heads, which you'll notice is you put it into turns real hard (just remember that going into turns, you do not want to let up abruptly on the gas, car should be neutral or with some power).||||reg||1
